    '**SUBMISSION TO THE DAMASCUS TOURISM LICENSING COMMITTEE · Hotel Barada, licence 4471 · 11 October · H. Alloush, Deputy Manager**',
    '**WHAT WE APPLY FOR.** **A twelve-month exemption under article 14(2) from the requirement for an addressable fire-detection panel, to run to 30 November next year, decided before our renewal date of 1 December.** **In the alternative, and if the committee is not minded to grant an exemption, a phased compliance date of 1 June with a written report to the committee at three months.**',
    '**WHAT WE ACCEPT, WITHOUT QUALIFICATION.** **Nine of the eleven findings in the inspection report of 28 September are correct and we do not contest them: findings 1, 2, 3, 5, 6, 8, 9, 10 and 11.** **Seven of the nine have been closed, with dates below. Two remain open and have dates against them.** **We say this on the first page because the committee should know before it reads anything else that we are contesting two findings and not an inspection.**',
    '**WHAT HAS ALREADY BEEN DONE, WITH DATES.** **Panel surveyed and quoted, 4 August. Order placed with Nahas Systems, 11 August. Installation booked, 22 January, which is the earliest date the installer will give for a panel of this type.** **Interim measures in place since 6 August: the night porter’s round extended to the basement and the third floor at 01.00 and 04.00, initialled on the sheet, and the sheet available for inspection at any hour without notice.** **Finding 4 (guest register retention) closed 2 October. Finding 7 (extractor service) is addressed below.**',
    '**THE TWO FINDINGS WE CONTEST.** **Finding 4 as drafted records that guest registers were unavailable for March. They were produced to the inspector on the day in the box file she examined second; her note refers to the April file.** **We attach the March register and ask that the finding be withdrawn rather than closed, because a closed finding stays on the record and this one did not happen.** **Finding 7 records the kitchen extractor as last serviced in February. The certificate attached is dated 3 July and was issued by the contractor the committee itself approves.**',
